eference — `_add_argument_calls`, `_option_record`, `scan_cli`, `build_cli_reference`, `_cli_doc_exit`, its marker pair and its `--cli-doc` flag. It rides THIS module rather than a new `gen_cli_reference.py` on the ruling's own words and on the one-home rule: it is the same AST walk `scan_inventory` already does, one step further, over the same `_walk_roots`/`module_contracts`/`splice_region` the file owns — a second module would have duplicated all four and owed a new LLR/TC/IF chain for a surface this one already declares. Freezing it here is the ra\r\n     \"gen_arch_map.py\": 1433,  # +39 SLOC (1394 -> 1433) 2026-09-01, WI-543 REVIEW-A round-2 rework: the shared checker now diffs bootstrap.delivery_inventory physical sources/reasoned exclusions against MAPPING, inherits generator references for derived outputs, and reports an omitted real shipped source as gate-class missing_file; helper extraction kept every function below the C901 floor. Reviewed bump, reason in docs/log.d/WI-543-sr163-verification-tc.md. Earlier: +53 SLOC (1341 -> 1394) 2026-09-01, WI-543 rework (REVIEW-A MAJOR): the checker gains a DELIVERED path — `mapping_purpose_over_repo` assembles the real inventory/spine/absences and grades them, wired into `main` as the warn-fir\r\n-    \"check.py\": 1309,  # +8 (1301 -> 1309) 2026-10-21, WI-969 (P7): the `adoption-record` pre-commit step, its step tuple and comment and its `BUILTIN_STEP_NAMES` row, whose body is `adoption_record.py` (the `plan-gate` shape). NOT DECOMPOSABLE here: the step table is this module's one home for built-in steps. Reviewed bump, reason in the WI-969 plan (P7). Earlier: +3 (1298 -> 1301) 2026-10-18, WI-925: changed_paths maps an undeclared trunk to changes unknown, so every opted-in step runs. Reviewed bump, reason in docs/decisions/wi-925.toml. Earlier: RE-STAMPED DOWN -9 (1307 -> 1298) 2026-10-18, WI-915: docs/stack.ini is parsed in one place, kitlib.config.read_stack_ini; load_profile and _ge\r\n+    \"check.py\": 1340,  #